{
  "tema": 5225,
  "slug": "vine-viniste-vino",
  "titulo": "Venir in the preterite",
  "subtitulo": "¿Por qué no viniste ayer?",
  "foto": "t02.jpg",
  "regla": "Venir is irregular in the preterite: stem vin- + -e, -iste, -o, -imos, -ieron, with no written accents: vine, viniste, vino, vinimos, vinieron.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": null,
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Venir** (_to come_) changes its stem to **vin-** in the preterite."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "It takes the irregular endings **-e, -iste, -o, -imos, -ieron**, with **no written accents**: **vine**, **vino**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Person",
            "venir"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "yo",
              "vine"
            ],
            [
              "tú",
              "viniste"
            ],
            [
              "él / ella / usted",
              "vino"
            ],
            [
              "nosotros",
              "vinimos"
            ],
            [
              "ellos / ellas / ustedes",
              "vinieron"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Watch **nosotros**: present **venimos**, preterite **vinimos**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Verbs built on venir work the same: **convenir** → **convino**, **intervenir** → **intervino**, **prevenir** → **previno**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **él vino** (_he came_) is spelled just like **vino** (_wine_). Easy to remember."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "¿A qué hora ==vino== el plomero?",
              "en": "What time did the plumber come?"
            },
            {
              "es": "Hoy ==vine== a la playa a las seis para agarrar las mejores olas.",
              "en": "Today I came to the beach at six to catch the best waves."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿Por qué no ==viniste== al entrenamiento de jiu-jitsu?",
              "en": "Why didn't you come to jiu-jitsu practice?"
            },
            {
              "es": "Mis primos ==vinieron== de Ensenada para la boda.",
              "en": "My cousins came from Ensenada for the wedding."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Vinimos== en camión porque el carro no arrancó.",
              "en": "We came by bus because the car wouldn't start."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿Ustedes ==vinieron== solos o con sus hijos?",
              "en": "Did you come alone or with your kids?"
            },
            {
              "es": "Nadie ==vino== a la junta del huerto comunitario.",
              "en": "Nobody came to the community garden meeting."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "trampa",
      "titulo": "The trap",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "pares",
          "lista": [
            {
              "filas": [
